>> title: Roasted Brussels Sprouts, Air Fryer
>> category: Vegetables & Sides
>> tags: brussels sprouts, air fryer, basket, side, balsamic
>> counters: The Air Fryer & the Pot
>> dish: roasted-brussels-sprouts
>> kit: Air Fryer
>> aka: air fryer brussels sprouts, basket sprouts, crispy air fryer sprouts, air fried brussels sprouts
>> servings: 4
>> time: 35 min
>> slack: forgiving — the loose leaves char five minutes before the halves are done and that is the best part, so late costs nothing here
>> washing-up: the basket, the bowl
>> capacity: 4 — one 5.7 L air fryer basket, roast, air fry
>> keeps: not at all — the loose charred leaves were the best part and they are soft by morning

>> step: Written for a preheated 5.7 L basket. From cold, add three minutes. A 3.5 L basket is two batches, not more minutes.
Every loose leaf that falls off goes in. Here they crisp instead of burning.

>> step: halve through the root, toss in the bowl, loose leaves and all
Halve @Brussels sprouts{1%lb}(450 g; trimmed) through the root and toss in a #bowl{} with @olive oil{1%Tbs}(15 mL), @kosher salt{1%tsp}, @black pepper{1/2%tsp}.

>> step: roast in the basket 175°C (350°F), 20–25 min, one layer cut side down
Roast @&(~1)halved sprouts{} in a preheated #air fryer basket{} at 175°C (350°F) for ~air fry{22%min}, one layer and cut side down.

>> step: toss the basket at twelve minutes — a loose rattle, not a wet thud
Toss @&(~1)sprouts{} by shaking the basket once.

>> step: toss hot in the same bowl, off the heat
Toss @&(~1)roasted sprouts{} with @balsamic vinegar{1%Tbs}(15 mL), @honey{1%tsp}, @flaky salt{1/2%tsp}.

>> step: A test kitchen tried 200°C on these and threw it out: the outside browned before the inside softened.
Lower and longer, which is the opposite of what conversion charts say.
